/**
 * Multilingual keyword lexicon (EN, DE, FR, ES, IT, some NL/PT) mapping text to
 * fields of study. Used for everything a person consumes (video titles, channel
 * descriptions, podcasts, subreddits, repos, search queries) and, by the
 * scrapers, for programme names that come without a usable subject code.
 *
 * Syntax per entry, separated by `|`:
 *   term          exact token or phrase (phrases match consecutive tokens)
 *   term:2.5      with weight (default 1)
 *   stem*         token prefix   (`neuro*` matches neuroscience, neuronal, ...)
 *   *suffix       token suffix   (`*informatik` matches Wirtschaftsinformatik)
 *   =AI           case-sensitive token, checked against the original text, for
 *                 abbreviations that are ordinary words in other languages
 *                 (Italian "ai", French "j'ai")
 *
 * Terms are normalised like the text (lowercase, accents stripped, punctuation
 * to spaces), so umlauts and accents may be written as usual.
 *
 * Weights: 3 = unambiguous ("organic chemistry", "Maschinenbau"), 2 = strong,
 * 1 = suggestive, below 1 = weak hint that only counts in company. Names of
 * channels and creators that are strongly tied to one subject are included as
 * phrases, since channel titles run through the same matcher.
 */
